Code Red: code moves (the battle rule, approved tentatively 2026-10-08). When a Pokémon
gets to use a move, the host has it write the move's code and runs it on the target's
bytes: hit = FireRed carries on as usual (accuracy roll included); miss = the move fails
and the text box says why (crashed / wrong / too long / no code). Both sides.
Host-optional: no host, no reply in time, or a cancelled request = plain FireRed.
Replaces byte battles v1 (damage from script output); damage is FireRed's again.
